    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "b202d929-b73c-3b54-88f4-a90e204a84d0",
                "word": "chthonic",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "21b293be-12b8-41d0-8b26-7db7b2748388",
                        "entry_id": "b202d929-b73c-3b54-88f4-a90e204a84d0",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more chthonic"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "3bd54553-fe0b-4840-8647-0d5f928a974d",
                        "entry_id": "b202d929-b73c-3b54-88f4-a90e204a84d0",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most chthonic"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "11e9352f-33dd-339d-9bb2-4a0c1fb79f60",
                        "entry_id": "b202d929-b73c-3b54-88f4-a90e204a84d0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dwelling within the underworld."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3258c10a-66e7-4999-815e-2ba5e9b14724",
                                "sense_id": "11e9352f-33dd-339d-9bb2-4a0c1fb79f60",
                                "text": "The young pantheon had remanded their elders to the role of smouldering, chthonic gods; to inhabiting dark, deep places, hidden from mortal eyes and influence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71ee89bd-0141-4a46-8b45-42475740282e",
                                "sense_id": "11e9352f-33dd-339d-9bb2-4a0c1fb79f60",
                                "text": "In this ceremony the Olympian Gods are placed in opposition to the Chthonic genii, the divinities of death and the dark side of nature, in which class the heroes are also reckoned; but Zeus Soter is conceived as a third and lord over both worlds."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e656240-e27a-4a7a-a8b8-37fd585fefda",
                                "sense_id": "11e9352f-33dd-339d-9bb2-4a0c1fb79f60",
                                "text": "In connexion with these Chthonic surroundings, the form of the head-dress which crowns the recumbent figure of Dionysos-Pluto, and is also occasionally seen on the kead of the Kourotrophos at the foot of the couch, is of considerable significance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de9c69d8-b35d-4c4a-b7b2-1c809f84be3d",
                                "sense_id": "11e9352f-33dd-339d-9bb2-4a0c1fb79f60",
                                "text": "There is no god more chthonic than the god of death, Leinth, and it is he that holds on his left knee Maris Halna, who (in mere innocence) shows no fear of him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "39e28849-0fc7-4de2-93a4-ce83c51e18bb",
                                "sense_id": "11e9352f-33dd-339d-9bb2-4a0c1fb79f60",
                                "text": "The snake symbolizes the chthonic force, the being which crawls along the ground; the bird symbolizes the higher realms of the consciousness, the being which is liberated from earth and can fly off to Heaven."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9a90ba2-cd3e-4a8e-a533-46d1df5cb7a6",
                                "sense_id": "11e9352f-33dd-339d-9bb2-4a0c1fb79f60",
                                "text": "Beowulf's mood as he gets ready to fight the dragon - who could be read as a projection of Beowulf's own chthonic wisdom refined in the crucible of experience - recalls the mood of other tragic heroes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cece5ebd-d477-4705-a9b7-ee8ce2062a59",
                                "sense_id": "11e9352f-33dd-339d-9bb2-4a0c1fb79f60",
                                "text": "[H. Patrick] Glenn refers to Indigenous law as chthonic law, because it is the law of chthonic peoples – peoples 'who live ecological lives by being chthonic, that is, by living in or in close harmony with the earth'."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92dca1dd-b9e5-468e-bd2a-2a00e118e67d",
                                "sense_id": "11e9352f-33dd-339d-9bb2-4a0c1fb79f60",
                                "text": "A most striking thing about Hainin’s fauna is how chthonic it is."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "536f77fb-6cb0-4968-842d-92676d0c7414",
                        "source_entry_id": "b202d929-b73c-3b54-88f4-a90e204a84d0",
                        "source_sense_id": "11e9352f-33dd-339d-9bb2-4a0c1fb79f60",
                        "source_sense_description": "dwelling within or under the earth",
                        "target_lang_word": "chthonien",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chthonien",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe067b3d-977f-3fe5-8d75-f43532c91e10",
                                        "entry_id": "83d8f9b3-51b2-31ea-ba87-3e19452f8c3c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dans la mythologie grecque, relatif aux divinités infernales ou telluriques, c’est-à-dire souterraines, par opposition aux divinités ouraniennes ou éoliennes, c’est-à-dire célestes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f2cdc33-8d01-43d6-999d-6eec61b860d2",
                                                "sense_id": "fe067b3d-977f-3fe5-8d75-f43532c91e10",
                                                "text": "Ainsi, aux raisons théologiques qui partout enveloppaient de silence et d’ombre le culte des puissances chthoniennes, se joignaient, à Eleusis en particulier, des raisons historiques et politiques plus que suffisantes pour expliquer le secret des mystères, sans qu’il soit besoin d’imaginer une opposition quelconque entre les cultes mystiques et les formes publiques de la religion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c8c10af-7a4f-3165-9ceb-d7786b0435e2",
                                        "entry_id": "83d8f9b3-51b2-31ea-ba87-3e19452f8c3c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Plus largement, relatif aux déités du monde souterrain de toutes les mythologies."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bac36bb7-048e-497c-868f-2165a5a2666a",
                                                "sense_id": "4c8c10af-7a4f-3165-9ceb-d7786b0435e2",
                                                "text": "Le peuple hébreu, lui-même, a passé par l’idolâtrie et les cultes des dieux chthoniens, avant de transformer son Javeh en ce dieu fulminant que Moïse ne pouvait regarder face à face et qui nous éblouit encore dans la poésie d’Isaïe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bd377dc-5d6b-42cf-9435-f2a8f84a83f5",
                                                "sense_id": "4c8c10af-7a4f-3165-9ceb-d7786b0435e2",
                                                "text": "Les peuplades qui vivent au bord des grands lacs ou de la mer situent souvent sous les eaux le séjour des âmes, et il est possible qu’il y ait dans toutes ces traditions de villes sous-marines comme un ressouvenir lointain de cette conception ; il faut remarquer au reste qu’il existe souvent entre les divinités marines et les divinités funéraires d’étroites liaisons ; le rôle des dieux de la mer est souvent analogue à celui des dieux chthoniens, presque toujours investis de fonctions funèbres ; un des meilleurs exemples qu’on en puisse donner, c’est la place que tiennent les Sirènes et les Néréides dans la décoration des tombeaux grecs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1ac59fb3-7d5f-488a-9bb1-0191dc6a68e6",
                        "source_entry_id": "b202d929-b73c-3b54-88f4-a90e204a84d0",
                        "source_sense_id": "11e9352f-33dd-339d-9bb2-4a0c1fb79f60",
